-- ============================================================================
-- SC4 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Offshore & Marine Logistics, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/marine/beginner.
--
-- What this tier owns: VOYAGES, CAPACITY AND THE BINDING CONSTRAINT. Offshore
-- supply as a system and the sources with their editions, licences and read
-- dates; milk runs and dedicated voyages, legs and sailing hours, port and
-- field time; the stated weather factor and the activities it slows; fuel by
-- activity and the fuel bill; deck area and its usable fraction, deck load,
-- deadweight and the tanks; utilisation, the binding constraint and an
-- overloaded voyage.
--
-- AN APP COURSE. The Suite app is the Marine Logistics Planner; the practicals
-- also run in the course's own voyage and fleet calculator. The capstone grades
-- six values of this tier, each identical under every reading the engine states
-- and never a Monte Carlo draw.
-- ============================================================================

values ('marine', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-offshore-supply-as-a-system","title":"Offshore Supply as a System","lesson_keys":["l01-why-offshore-supply-is-planned","l02-sources-and-the-dates-they-were-read","l03-the-ekene-cluster-and-its-supply-base","l04-nautical-miles-knots-hours-and-tonnes","l05-calculator-panels-and-refusals"]},{"key":"m02-routes-and-voyage-time","title":"Routes and Voyage Time","lesson_keys":["l01-milk-runs-and-dedicated-voyages","l02-legs-and-sailing-hours","l03-port-and-field-time","l04-the-voyage-in-days"]},{"key":"m03-weather-and-fuel","title":"Weather and Fuel","lesson_keys":["l01-a-stated-weather-factor","l02-which-activities-the-weather-slows","l03-fuel-burn-by-activity","l04-the-fuel-bill"]},{"key":"m04-deck-and-bulk-capacity","title":"Deck and Bulk Capacity","lesson_keys":["l01-deck-area-in-square-metres","l02-the-usable-fraction-of-the-deck","l03-deck-load-and-deadweight","l04-bulk-tanks-by-product"]},{"key":"m05-the-binding-constraint","title":"The Binding Constraint","lesson_keys":["l01-utilisation-per-constraint","l02-the-binding-constraint-and-its-ties","l03-an-overloaded-voyage","l04-a-tank-the-vessel-does-not-have","l05-reading-a-voyage-plan"]},{"key":"m06-planning-a-voyage-end-to-end","title":"Planning a Voyage End to End","lesson_keys":["l01-a-psv-and-an-ahts-on-one-route","l02-calm-and-rainy-season","l03-checking-a-plan-before-it-sails","l04-the-capstone-brief"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
